# Poing live: the AlphaTheta OMNIS-DUO as a MIDI controller.
#
# The numbers come from rekordbox 7.2.19's own controller map for the DUO
# (MidiMappings/OMNIS-DUO.midi.csv); docs/LIVE.md says how to read it and
# what each control does in Poing.
#
# One control per line:  status data1 action [deck] [argument] [options]
#   status  the first byte, channel included (90 = note on ch1, B4 = CC ch5)
#   data1   the note or CC number
#   deck    1 or 2 (absent for the mixer's master controls and the effects)
#   options hires   a 14-bit fader: its LSB comes on CC data1+0x20
#           invert  the fader the other way round
#           noled   do not light this control
# A note-on with velocity 0 is a release, like a note-off. Buttons and pads
# with a state are lit by sending the same message back (7F on, 00 off).
#
# To fix a control without rebuilding Poing, copy this file to Poing's
# config folder (%APPDATA%\Poing\omnis-duo.map on Windows) and edit it there.
# Poing logs every message from the DUO it does not know:
#   poing: live: unmapped 96 04 7F

# MIDI ports whose name contains this play the decks.
port OMNIS

# ---- deck 1 (channel 1, pads on channel 6)
90 00 play 1
90 01 cue 1
90 05 start 1
90 1F sync 1
90 51 load 1
95 00 hotcue 1 1
95 01 hotcue 1 2
95 02 hotcue 1 3
95 03 hotcue 1 4
95 04 loop 1 1
95 05 loop 1 2
95 06 loop 1 4
95 07 loop 1 8
95 08 mute 1 vocals
95 09 mute 1 drums
95 0A mute 1 bass
95 0B mute 1 other
90 0C section 1 -1
90 0B section 1 1
90 43 loop_toggle 1
90 44 loop_toggle 1
B0 2E loop_size 1
90 20 touch 1
90 48 touch 1
B0 22 scratch 1
B0 21 nudge 1
B0 26 nudge 1
B0 00 tempo 1 hires
B0 02 level 1

# ---- deck 2 (channel 2, pads on channel 7)
91 00 play 2
91 01 cue 2
91 05 start 2
91 1F sync 2
91 51 load 2
96 00 hotcue 2 1
96 01 hotcue 2 2
96 02 hotcue 2 3
96 03 hotcue 2 4
96 04 loop 2 1
96 05 loop 2 2
96 06 loop 2 4
96 07 loop 2 8
96 08 mute 2 vocals
96 09 mute 2 drums
96 0A mute 2 bass
96 0B mute 2 other
91 0C section 2 -1
91 0B section 2 1
91 43 loop_toggle 2
91 44 loop_toggle 2
B1 2E loop_size 2
91 20 touch 2
91 48 touch 2
B1 22 scratch 2
B1 21 nudge 2
B1 26 nudge 2
B1 00 tempo 2 hires
B1 02 level 2

# ---- mixer (channel 5)
B4 01 trim 1
B4 02 eq_high 1
B4 03 eq_mid 1
B4 04 eq_low 1
B4 05 color 1
B4 11 fader 1
B4 06 trim 2
B4 07 eq_high 2
B4 08 eq_mid 2
B4 09 eq_low 2
B4 0A color 2
B4 12 fader 2
B4 0B xfader

# ---- beat FX (channel 5, buttons as CCs)
B4 72 fx_on
B4 34 fx_select
B4 5B fx_depth
B4 4C fx_beats -1
B4 4D fx_beats 1

# ---- on the DUO, not used by Poing (so they are not logged as unmapped)
# shift (the DUO sends shifted pads, cue and loop as their own notes)
90 3F ignore
91 3F ignore
# jog search (shift + jog), needle search, the touch panel's master, quantize,
# slip, vinyl, master tempo and auto cue buttons
B0 29 ignore
B1 29 ignore
B0 1C ignore
B1 1C ignore
90 1E ignore
91 1E ignore
90 09 ignore
91 09 ignore
90 2B ignore
91 2B ignore
90 12 ignore
91 12 ignore
90 11 ignore
91 11 ignore
90 0F ignore
91 0F ignore
# headphone cue, crossfader curve, beat FX auto/tap (shift + beat), browse
B4 46 ignore
B4 47 ignore
B4 5F ignore
B4 78 ignore
B4 79 ignore
B4 4F ignore
B4 60 ignore
90 33 ignore
90 61 ignore
